{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s49-p01",
      "text": "When cold weather comes, many birds move to the south.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p02",
      "text": "Many animals do not remain in one place.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p03",
      "text": "Moving is a normal part of their lives.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p04-01",
      "text": "Some move to find food more easily,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p04-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p04-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p04-02",
      "text": "but others move to get away from crowded places or to survive disasters like an earthquake.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p04-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p04-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p05",
      "text": "We can compare this action to people moving for better opportunities.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p06",
      "text": "Some fishes give birth in warm water and move to cold water to feed.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p07",
      "text": "The most famous migration is probably that of the fish called salmon.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p08",
      "text": "This fish is usually grey, but turns red when it is ready to breed.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p09",
      "text": "It is born in fresh water but travels miles to salt water.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p10-01",
      "text": "They must fight against the strong force of the river and avoid being hunted by bears,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p10-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p10-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p10-02",
      "text": "because the law of nature allows only the strongest salmon to survive.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p10-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p10-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p11",
      "text": "When it is old, it returns to its birthplace in fresh water.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p12",
      "text": "Then it gives birth and dies.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p13",
      "text": "In the north of Europe, there is a kind of mouse.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p14",
      "text": "They usually look pale, but when their homes become crowded, their colour gets brighter.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p15",
      "text": "They have a crazy way of moving.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p16",
      "text": "Sometimes they move all the way to the seaside, forming large groups like an army.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p17",
      "text": "Many of them are killed when they fall into the sea.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p18",
      "text": "Recently, scientists have studied a special kind of lobsters.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p19-01",
      "text": "Every year, when the season of bad weather arrives,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p19-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p19-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p19-02",
      "text": "the lobsters get into a long line and start to walk across the floor of the ocean, just like soldiers marching.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p19-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p19-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p20",
      "text": "Nobody knows where they go.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p21",
      "text": "The reason why animals move may vary.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s49-p22",
      "text": "Maybe living things just like to travel.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p22.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s49-p22.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
